      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Another solar company backed out of installing our solar system because of the extra work required by the nature of the tiles on our roof.This put me in a rush late December to find another installer so I could get the maximum solar rebate. Online I found Sync Energy which is a WA based company operating state based depots using local installers. The price for supply and installation was $100 cheaper than the previous good offer.The installation was done with little delay by a 10 year qualified installer with 2 helpers who did an excellent job. They were punctual and polite and cleaned up thoroughly after the job.In terms of Solarquotes measures of a good installation the job was done by a fully qualified technician who only did the one job on this day. Metal covers were installed over roof DC switches, stainless steel bolts were used to avoid galvanic reactions and cables were protected.Sync Energy arranged for our meter to be exchanged with our electricity supplier.All round we had an excellent job done at an unbeatable price and are very pleased with our purchase.Highly recommended.",
